cdi wrote:
> As for the Castle ... until I'm absolutely certain I have magic
> resistance or can blessed genocide 'L' ... this is out.

If you have a spare wand of striking, It's pretty easy to test that
cloak. When you zap yourself with a wand of striking, you will always
get the "Boing!" message if you have MR. If you don't have MR, you'll
always bash yourself for a max of 24 damage (even if you have magic
cancellation). None of your other armor can grant MR, so if the wand
boings, you must have a [CoMR.

> So here's the plan:
>
> a) Take care of Medusa, then blank a bunch of potions.
> b) Go up and use the /oDeath on the mind flayer.
> c) Grab the bones pile loot and run like hell for Minetown.
> d) Figure out where to go from there.

I think that's basically a good plan. Stepping into Gehennom with bad
AC is not something I'd do if I had any other alternatives. It only
takes one summoning <foo>lich to really ruin your day. They always seem
to summon minotaurs, and those things can *really* pound you, even with
decent AC.

You might consider other methods of dealing with the mind flayer,
though. They have a base MR of 90, so you can burn through several
charges without even touching it. If there aren't many charges are in
the wand, it could be a total waste. Personally, I'd just engrave/burn
the E word, levitate with your boots (assuming that they're
non-cursed), and start throwing things at it. If it gets within
punching distance, give it a few jabs while it turns to flee. They
aren't that hard to kill -- it's just the sucking that, er...sucks.

